Subject: [PATCH] glassine: xwayland: wm_fd[0] belongs to the xwm once it is handed over (double close)

The lazy-Xwayland hang came back (sway pid 7718): after an
Xwayland exit and a successful lazy re-arm, new X clients never woke sway.
a capture: of the three X0 listen fds (28 = abstract @/tmp/.X11-unix/X0,
29 = the path socket, 158 = a dup of 29), sway's epoll watched only 158,
the dup that wl_event_loop_add_fd made of x_fd[1]; the dup of x_fd[0] (the
abstract socket, which libxcb tries first) was gone, so a client's connect
sat in that backlog forever.

Cause: the ready event hands wm_fd[0] to the xwm (xcb_connect_to_fd), and
xcb_disconnect in xwm_destroy closes it, but server_finish_process closes
wm_fd[0] too. When Xwayland exits, its Wayland client and the xwm's X
connection both hang up; if the client destroy runs first,
server_finish_process frees that number, the lazy re-arm's first
wl_event_loop_add_fd (x_fd[0]) dups into it, and the xwm's HUP handler then
closes it in xcb_disconnect. Order-dependent, hence most cycles worked.
Fix: after the ready event, wm_fd[0] is no longer the server's.

--- a/xwayland/server.c
+++ b/xwayland/server.c
@@ -290,6 +290,16 @@
 		.wm_fd = server->wm_fd[0],
 	};
 	wl_signal_emit_mutable(&server->events.ready, &event);
+	/* glassine: the xwm owns wm_fd[0] now (xcb_connect_to_fd; xcb_disconnect closes
+	 * it). server_finish_process closed it again: a double close. When
+	 * Xwayland exits, the client destroy can run before the xwm's HUP: then
+	 * the lazy re-arm's first wl_event_loop_add_fd dup (the abstract @X0
+	 * socket) gets that just-freed number, and xwm_destroy's xcb_disconnect
+	 * closes it -> X clients connect to @X0 and hang forever, nobody watches
+	 * it (a capture epoll had only the X0 path socket's dup) */
+	if (!wl_list_empty(&server->events.ready.listener_list)) {
+		server->wm_fd[0] = -1;	/* (no listener: nobody took it, still ours) */
+	}
 
 	/* We removed the source, so don't need recheck */
 	return 0;
